4003e782b9085d3c4cecdcee9899fe01857bde30f7d7c9ea5e52cb9db3bdeac3 {"key": "4003e782b9085d3c4cecdcee9899fe01857bde30f7d7c9ea5e52cb9db3bdeac3", "original": {"closure_evidence": [], "counterexample": "A real Prepared instance exits after BeginTransaction and before TakeSnapshot. A fresh instance safely aborts and returns RolledBack, then exits. Another fresh instance acquires authority and RecoverOnStart blocks because no full baseline exists. The old SnapshottingAborted test has no Prepared port and only recovers once before directly beginning a new transaction.", "id": "IMPLEMENTATION-ABORT-TERMINAL-REOPEN-1", "obligation": "implementation", "paths": ["MultiplayerHoeingAssistant/Services/TaskCenter/MigrationSwitchTransaction.cs:2012", "MultiplayerHoeingAssistant/Services/TaskCenter/MigrationSwitchTransaction.cs:2025", "Test/MultiplayerHoeingAssistant.UnitTest/ServiceTests/TaskCenter/R56MigrationSwitchTransactionTests.cs:785"], "repair_steps": ["Represent and validate the no-baseline/no-data-operation safe-abort terminal distinctly. A new instance may verify its pending/history/journal relationship and observe read-only without fabricating historical S0.", "Keep full fresh-root checks for complete-baseline RolledBack. Corrupt evidence or existing data operations must never obtain an abort exemption."], "root_cause": "A no-baseline safe abort publishes RolledBack with ControlledBaseline absent. The next Prepared instance's RecoverOnStart unconditionally calls RefreshControlledWitness for RolledBack, which reports controlled_root_baseline_missing and changes that legitimate terminal back to Blocked.", "severity": "important", "status": "open", "tests": ["Prepared Begin->exit->safe-abort recovery->exit->second recovery->new transaction, with bytes/identity unchanged, no Applied and no production Action.", "Cover partial snapshot-copy failure and reject an abort exemption when data/journal exists. Mutate terminal classification or remove the legitimate abort-resume branch 